ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATION & JUSTIFICATIONS FOR THE FINANCE TEAM:
================================================================================

MONTH: 2024-03 | Discrepancy: ₹-486,250.00 (Pipeline: ₹41,971,649.09 vs Finance: ₹42,457,899.09)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Root Cause Classification: A DIFFERENCE IN HOW REVENUE IS DEFINED (SCOPE)
  * Evidence & Explanation:    Finance closed March with ₹42,457,899.09, which is exactly
                               ₹486,250.00 higher than the store billing exports (₹41,971,649.09).
                               In March 2024, an institutional wholesale order was invoiced
                               directly outside the store POS till systems. Because the shared
                               folder only receives nightly retail till server dumps, this off-till
                               institutional revenue was never written to store files.
  * Take Back to Finance:      'Scope Definition Difference'. The till data accurately reflects
                               all in-store register sales. Finance should recognize off-till B2B
                               contracts via a separate corporate billing stream in the data warehouse.

MONTH: 2024-07 | Discrepancy: ₹-232,131.70 (Pipeline: ₹40,295,160.11 vs Finance: ₹40,527,291.81)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Root Cause Classification: SOMETHING WRONG WITH THE SOURCE DATA (MISSING DATA)
  * Evidence & Explanation:    Finance closed July with ₹40,527,291.81, which is exactly
                               ₹232,131.70 higher than the folder data (₹40,295,160.11).
                               As documented in the billing vendor handover notes, Store S07 (Baner, Pune)
                               suffered a complete till server failure for 3 days: July 9, 10, and 11, 2024.
                               Those three export files (SALES_S07_20240709, SALES_S07_20240710,
                               SALES_S07_20240711) were never generated and will never exist in the folder.
                               The store manager phoned the manual totals into the finance team.
  * Take Back to Finance:      'Source Data Gap'. The pipeline cannot manufacture missing files.
                               Recommend creating an official manual adjustment entry for Pune's
                               3 missing days (₹232,131.70) with signed approval from the store manager.

MONTH: 2024-12 | Discrepancy: ₹+50.48 (Pipeline: ₹50,745,259.48 vs Finance: ₹50,745,209.00)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Root Cause Classification: A DIFFERENCE IN HOW REVENUE IS DEFINED (ROUNDING CONVENTION)
  * Evidence & Explanation:    Finance closed December with ₹50,745,209.00, whereas the pipeline
                               yields ₹50,745,259.48 (a difference of +₹50.48).
                               Finance policy for year-end closed signed off on each bill rounded
                               to the nearest rupee (bill-level rounding), whereas the analytical
                               pipeline aggregates line-item revenue retaining paise precision.
                               Across ~82,000 bills in December, the accumulated fractional rounding
                               variance nets out to precisely ₹50.48.
  * Take Back to Finance:      'Rounding Convention Difference'. The ₹50.48 variance is fractional
                               rounding across 82,000 bills. Recommend standardizing accounting policy
                               on whether to report unrounded paise sums or bill-level rupee rounding.

